  curator: fix_butanediol_duplicate
  action: MERGED_FROM
  changes: 'Absorbed ''Butane-1,4-diol''. `Butane-1,4-diol` was created by the #308
    comma-split repair, which rejoined the fragments `Butane-1` and `4-diol` and grounded
    them to CHEBI:41189 — without checking whether MIM already held that term. It
    did: `1,4-Butanediol`. So the repair produced a second live record for one compound,
    which is the duplicate-shadowing defect this session has been fixing elsewhere
    (#334/#347). Merged into the pre-existing record; the two fragment labels are
    kept as RAW_TEXT synonyms so the comma-split provenance survives.'
  llm_assisted: false
